The attached image displays confocal microscopy results of skeletal muscle 24 hours post-injection, demonstrating Nano-11's role in inducing inflammation and cellular uptake at the injection site. The top row, representing Nano-11 with OVA, shows robust recruitment of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages, MHCII+ cells, and 1A8+ neutrophils (all green), with AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) clearly visible within these recruited cells. In contrast, the bottom row, showing soluble OVA alone, reveals minimal inflammatory cell infiltration. This visualization confirms that Nano-11 enhances the delivery of adsorbed antigens to key immune cells in vivo, which is a critical step for initiating an effective immune response as a vaccine adjuvant.